
<p>Nick Heer, Pixel Envy:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>There are a whole bunch of features and fixes coming to Safari
with Apple’s OS 27.3 update. One that is not in the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-27_3-release-notes">beta release
notes</a> but appears nevertheless is support for <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Privacy_Control#Legal_status">Global
Privacy Control</a>. This new standard is effectively a
<a href="https://pxlnv.com/linklog/rip-dnt-firefox/">replacement for Do Not Track</a> with legal muscle that
<a href="https://pxlnv.com/linklog/webxray-opt-out-audit/">should</a> permit you to indicate your tracking preference
one time and then, theoretically, never again see a cookie
consent banner.</p>
</blockquote>

